{"type":"message","id":"81041335","parentId":"7abf2a68","timestamp":"2026-05-26T05:42:32.011Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"write_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/tmp/crypto-run-20260526-053909/research/raw.json","content":"{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"story_id\": \"ondo-finance-founder-nathan-allman-dies-aged-32\",\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Ondo Finance Founder Nathan Allman Passes Away Unexpectedly at 32\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"Ondo Finance Nathan Allman\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Ondo Finance Founder and CEO Nathan Allman Dies Suddenly at 32\",\n  \"primary_asset\": \"Ondo Finance\",\n  \"chart_coin\": \"ondo-finance\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinTelegraph\",\n    \"Blockhead\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/ondo-finance-founder-nathan-allman-passes-away-aged-32\",\n    \"https://blockhead.co/2026/05/26/ondo-finance-ceo-nathan-allman-dies-unexpectedly\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Nathan Allman, the founder and CEO of real-world asset (RWA) tokenization platform Ondo Finance, has passed away unexpectedly at the age of 32.\",\n    \"Ondo Finance officially announced his passing on May 26, 2026, stating that his brilliance, humility, and drive shaped every part of what Ondo is today.\",\n    \"Company president Ian De Bode, who joined Ondo in late 2023 and became president in November 2025, has been appointed as the new CEO immediately.\",\n    \"Allman founded Ondo Finance in 2021 after previously working in Goldman Sachs' digital asset team and studying at Brown University and Stanford. He was widely recognized as a pioneer in bringing US Treasuries, stocks, and debt onto blockchain networks.\",\n    \"Under Allman's leadership, Ondo brought $3.86 billion in tokenized real-world assets on-chain, capturing the attention of institutional giants like BlackRock.\",\n    \"Ondo's governance token (ONDO) fell about 3% following the announcement, trading near $0.43, with the community and leadership mourning the loss while pledging to continue his vision.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Ondo Finance founder and CEO Nathan Allman has passed away unexpectedly at the age of 32, the company announced on May 26, 2026. Under his leadership, Ondo Finance had grown into one of the largest tokenized real-world asset (RWA) platforms in the world. Nathan Allman, a pioneer of blockchain tokenization, was key in helping Ondo bring over $3.86 billion worth of tokenized real-world assets on-chain, including U.S. Treasuries, stocks, and commodities, serving over 111,680 token holders.\\n\\nFollowing the unexpected announcement, Ondo Finance released an official statement: 'It is with profound sadness that we announce the unexpected passing of Nathan Allman, Ondo's founder. Our hearts are with his family and loved ones. Nate’s brilliance, humility, and drive shaped every part of what Ondo is today. His belief in the power of technology to create a more open, accessible financial system lives on in everything we build. The impact he had on this industry, and on all of us personally, cannot be overstated.'\\n\\nAllman founded Ondo in 2021 after working on Goldman Sachs' digital assets desk. Prior to Goldman Sachs, he founded the crypto hedge fund ChainStreet Capital, which focused on algorithmic, event-driven trading. He was an alumnus of Brown University and Stanford. The tokenization movement that Allman contributed to helped capture the attention of Wall Street giants such as BlackRock, who see potential in the technology to make trading and settlement more efficient.\\n\\nOndo announced that the company's president, Ian De Bode, would serve as CEO immediately. De Bode joined Ondo as chief strategy officer in late 2023, having previously led digital assets work at McKinsey. His promotion to president in November 2025, followed now by the CEO appointment, reflects the organizational groundwork Allman had put in place.\\n\\n'It’s been an incredibly sad day for Ondo Finance,' De Bode told Cointelegraph. 'Nate was not only an incredible founder and visionary, but also a very close personal friend. He will be missed dearly. The mission of Ondo, Nate's mission, has not changed. If Nate were here, he would want to continue executing with excellence. We will make him proud.'\\n\\nOndo vice president and head of marketing, Ben Grossman, added that Allman 'was a once-in-a-generation founder and visionary. He was absolutely brilliant, with a vision and drive that shaped the industry and everyone around him. He will be enormously missed.' Ondo did not share further details on Allman’s death, and a spokesperson noted that his family has requested privacy at this time.\\n\\nONDO, the company's governance token, was trading at $0.43, down around 3% over the 24 hours following the announcement. Despite the sudden and tragic loss, the newly appointed CEO Ian De Bode and the management team emphasized that Ondo's roadmap and strategic mission remain steadfast to carry on Nathan Allman's pioneering legacy in decentralized and institutional finance.\"\n}"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":3994,"output":1212,"cacheRead":47750,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":52956,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779774146498,"responseId":"wzIVap3gPNax694Poou62QU"}}
